<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        A dashboard is a screen of live widgets, such as a clock, who's working today, announcements or the laser
        scoreboard. Dashboards can be your home screen, and can also be shown on kiosk TVs through a projection program.
    </FluentText>

    <HelpSection Title="The dashboards page">
        <FluentText>
            <a href="/manage/dashboards">Dashboards</a> shows every dashboard in your company as a card, with a small picture of
            its layout. Badges say which one is <strong>Your home screen</strong>, which is <strong>Everyone's home screen</strong>,
            and which are <strong>On a kiosk TV</strong>, with the projection program that shows it (and how many more, if
            there are others; hover over the badge to see them all).
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Viewing a dashboard live">
        <FluentText>
            Select <strong>View</strong> on a dashboard's card, or its layout picture, to open it on its own page. It works just
            like it does on a home screen: the widgets are live, and buttons and controls act.
        </FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li>Select <strong>Full screen</strong> to fill the whole screen with it, for example on a spare monitor or TV. A
                dashboard set to <strong>Fill the screen</strong> stretches to fill the screen, like on a kiosk TV.</li>
            <li>Press <strong>Esc</strong>, or select the small button in the bottom-right corner, to leave full screen.
                iPhones don't offer full screen, so the button isn't shown there.</li>
            <li>Managers and Admins also see <strong>Edit</strong>, to open the dashboard in the designer.</li>
        </ul>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Choosing your home screen">
        <FluentText>
            Select the house button on a dashboard to make it your home screen. Select it again to go back to the standard
            home page. You can also choose under <strong>Home Screen</strong> on your <a href="/account/manage">account page</a>.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Everyone's home screen">
        <FluentText>
            Managers and Admins can use the people button to make a dashboard <strong>Everyone's home screen</strong>.
            Anyone who has picked their own dashboard, or chosen the standard home page, keeps their choice.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Making, copying and deleting dashboards">
        <FluentText>Admins and Managers can:</FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li>Select <strong>New dashboard</strong>, give it a <strong>Name</strong>, and choose what it starts from:
                <strong>Blank</strong>, or a ready-made layout such as <strong>Staff home screen</strong>,
                <strong>Manager's morning</strong>, <strong>Front desk</strong> or <strong>Arena scoreboard TV</strong>.
                Select <strong>Create and open</strong> to go straight to the designer.</li>
            <li>Select <strong>Edit</strong>, or the layout picture, to change a dashboard. (For anyone else, the layout
                picture opens the live view.)</li>
            <li>Use the <strong>⋯</strong> button to <strong>Duplicate</strong> a dashboard (the copy is named "… (copy)")
                or <strong>Delete</strong> it.</li>
        </ul>
        <FluentText>Dashboards are shared across the company.</FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
